# Infrastructure

Only a `dev` environment exists. Add `prod` by copying `terraform/envs/dev` to
`terraform/envs/prod` (own state key, own GitHub environment and secrets) once real users or a
TestFlight build depend on it.

## Runtime (`deploy/`)

Docker Compose on a single host: API, PostgreSQL 18 and Caddy. The `deploy-dev` workflow builds
the API image, pushes it to GHCR and runs `docker compose up -d` over SSH as the `deploy` user in
`/opt/{{ project_slug }}`. First-time host setup (once):

1. Copy `deploy/compose.yaml`, `deploy/Caddyfile` and `deploy/env.example` (as `.env`, with real
   values) to `/opt/{{ project_slug }}/`.
2. `docker login ghcr.io` on the host with a token that can read packages.
3. Add `DEPLOY_HOST` and `DEPLOY_SSH_KEY` to the `dev` environment secrets in GitHub.
{% if infra_target == 'digitalocean' %}
## Terraform (`terraform/`)

`modules/host` creates the droplet (Docker preinstalled via cloud-init), a reserved IP, an SSH
key and a firewall. `envs/dev` instantiates it. State lives in a DigitalOcean Spaces bucket
(S3-compatible backend, see `envs/dev/backend.hcl`); create that bucket once by hand.

```bash
export DIGITALOCEAN_TOKEN=...            # or `doctl auth init`
export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...             # Spaces key, used by the S3 backend
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
terraform -chdir=infra/terraform/envs/dev init -backend-config=backend.hcl
terraform -chdir=infra/terraform/envs/dev plan
```

`terraform apply` runs only from CI (`.github/workflows/terraform.yml`) after merge; agents are
denied `apply`/`destroy` locally.
